{
  "name": "encoding-reflection-field-walk-through-a-method-value",
  "description": "The field walk of encoding-reflection names the reflect.Value method a call reaches through a method value or a method expression as it names a direct call's, and follows a reflect.Value through every value a local may hold and through the argument of each call of a function the program only calls by name. It judges every assertion on what Interface returns, whatever chain of reflect.Value methods produced the receiver. A walk through Field and Index, whatever their argument, constant FieldByIndex and FieldByName arguments, Elem on a pointer and no value of an interface type retains the methods the asserted interface requires on each type it computes, so a method nothing calls of a field's or an element's type is reported, and so is a method of a sibling field's type a constant index never reaches. Any other walk, Elem on an interface value among them, retains every method of every type reachable from the walked value's type. A value Interface returns that is printed rather than asserted is read by fmt's walk, which stops at its interface type, so its String method is reported.",
  "languages": ["go"],
  "target_kind": "application",
